  "guidebook": {
    "intro": "Kukanusha kwa Kiingereza hutumia neno moja dogo: **not**. Mara nyingi huja kama **don’t**, **doesn’t**, **didn’t** au **won’t**.",
    "phrases": [
      { "target": "I don’t want tea, thanks.", "base": "Sitaki chai, asante." },
      { "target": "It’s not true!", "base": "Si kweli!" },
      { "target": "I’m not a teacher.", "base": "Mimi si mwalimu." },
      { "target": "Not yet.", "base": "Bado." },
      { "target": "Maybe tomorrow.", "base": "Labda kesho." },
      { "target": "Yesterday I didn’t go to school.", "base": "Jana sikuenda shuleni." }
    ],
    "tips": [
      {
        "id": "dont-doesnt",
        "title": "Don’t na doesn’t",
        "body": [
          "Kiswahili hubadilisha kitenzi (**ninataka → sitaki**). Kiingereza huacha kitenzi na kuweka **don’t** mbele: **I want → I don’t want**.",
          "Kwa **he**, **she** na **it**, tumia **doesn’t**, na kitenzi hakiongezi -s: **He doesn’t want** (hataki), si “he doesn’t wants”."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "isnt",
        "title": "Si: isn’t, not",
        "body": [
          "**Si** ya Kiswahili ni **not** baada ya **am/is/are**: **I’m not a teacher** (mimi si mwalimu), **It isn’t true** (si kweli).",
          "**Bado** peke yake ni **not yet**. **Labda** ni **maybe**, na **hata kidogo** ni **not at all**."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "didnt-wont",
        "title": "Didn’t na won’t",
        "body": [
          "Kwa wakati uliopita, tumia **didn’t** na kitenzi cha msingi: **I went → I didn’t go** (sikuenda), **I ate → I didn’t eat** (sikula).",
          "Kwa wakati ujao, **will not** hufupishwa kuwa **won’t**: **I won’t go** (sitaenda)."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "culture": [
      {
        "title": "Kukataa kwa upole",
        "body": ["Kiingereza husema **No, thank you** au **I’m fine, thanks** kukataa kitu kwa adabu. **No** peke yake inaweza kusikika kali."]
      }
    ]
  },
